        "abstract": "Hydrogen degradation of GaAs devices is usually characterized as a mean-time-to-failure accelerated by temperature and hydrogen pressure. In gettered packages the hydrogen pressure can become negligible during a mission, leading to an undefined MTTF. A new metric, hydrogen exposure, E (atm-hr), with units of atmosphere-hours is introduced. Exposure is the product of hydrogen pressure and time, or more exactly, the time integral of the hydrogen partial pressure. Device reliability can then be unambiguously described by hydrogen exposure.",
