        "abstract": "The reliability of GaAs MIMCAPs is studied. The MIMCAPs have a low temperature PECVD nitride, Au metal electrodes and Ti adhesion layers. By examining the conduction properties of the SiN dielectric in these capacitors, a model is proposed to predict breakdown. A ramped voltage method is used to determine the extrinsic defect densities. The method for calculating failure rates from this model is shown, and voltage and temperature accelerated testing factors are derived.",
